      "text_raw": "Both models for the normalized transconductance to current ratio are plotted versus the inversion\ncoefficient in this slide. Both go through the same point at i=1. The difference is small. This is\nwhy the expression with the exponential will be used further.\nNote that, at an inversion coefficient of 8, where the V −V is 0.2 V, the normalized GM is\nGS T\nabout 1/3 of the maximum value in weak inversion. The corresponding g /I is about 4.2 V−1.\nm DS\nThis is nearly ten times less than for a bipolar transistor. In order to boost this ratio, we must\nchoose a smaller V −V . For a value of 0.15 V, the ratio g /I is already 5.4 V−1 and for\nGS T m DS\n0.1 V close to 7 V−1.",
